            <div xml:id="d103">

                <pb facs="0356" n="212" xml:id="pg212"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.77 Chinese Eastern/46: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">MacMurray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-07-19T11:00:00+08:00">July 19, 1929—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 12:25 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>590. Department’s 231, July 13, 3 [<hi rendition="#italic">1</hi>] p.m., repeated
                    to American Consul at Harbin who has replied as follows: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“July 17, 11 a.m. Local consular body has not held [and does not?]
                            contemplate at present holding meeting regarding present Soviet-Chinese
                            railway dispute. Japanese Consul General suggested to me yesterday
                            meeting to exchange views perhaps should be held if international
                            through traffic interrupted. Press advices from Harbin should be read
                            with caution.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">MacMurray</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
